    "title": "Delta Airlines Raises Bag Fees Due to Rising Fuel Costs",
    "text": "• Delta Airlines will increase checked bag fees on Wednesday.\n• The increase is due to rising fuel prices, attributed to the ongoing Iran conflict and the closure of the Strait of Hormuz.\n• The fee for the first checked bag on domestic flights will increase by $10 to $45.\n• The fee for the second checked bag on domestic flights will increase by $10 to $55.\n• The fee for a third checked bag will increase to $200.\n• Delta SkyMiles Medallion Members, First Class, Delta Premium Select and Delta One customers, active-duty military, and eligible co-branded Delta SkyMiles American Express Card holders will continue to receive complimentary checked bags.\n• JetBlue increased bag fees on March 30.\n• United Airlines raised bag fees on April 3.\n• President Donald Trump has warned Iran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz.\n• Americans are experiencing rising gas prices and interest rates.\n• A Goldman Sachs note suggested some Southeast Asian countries could run out of oil.\n• The U.S. could lose 60% of its fuel oil capacity.",
    "summary": "Another Airline Raises Bag Fees To Offset Fuel Costs As Iran War-Induced Oil Crisis Continues Delta Airlines will raise fees on checked bags Wednesday for passengers as fuel prices surge in the wake of the ongoing Iran war and closure of the Strait of Hormuz. “These updates are part of Delta’s ongoing review of pricing across its business and reflect the impact of evolving global conditions and industry dynamics.",
